  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": "homotopy-connections",
   "text": "Connect points"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Every continuous map f from a disk to Y can shrink to a constant: H(x,t) = f((1−t)x)."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "X = filled disk"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Input x"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Y = ring (annulus)"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Start f₀(x)"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Now fₜ(x)"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "id": null,
   "text": "End f₁(x)"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Same color = same input. Click or drag on a colored shape to circle corresponding points."
  },
  {
   "tag": "span",
   "id": null,
   "text": "The hatched hole is not part of Y."
  },
  {
   "tag": "summary",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Why?"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Move the input x toward the disk’s center, then apply the original map f. At t = 0 this gives f(x); at t = 1 every input gives f(0)."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "This works for any target space Y and any continuous starting map f: disk → Y. The outputs stay in Y because they are always outputs of f. You are deforming the map; Y itself stays fixed."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "The selector shows four sample maps. For the circle target, several inputs share each output; circle an input in X to follow its color."
  }
